{"jivajiva": [{"id": "jivAjiva", "headword": "जिवाजिव", "headword_slp1": "jivAjiva", "fold": "jivajiva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जिवाजिव m. The chakora bird.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जिवाजिवः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jivAjivaH"]}, {"id": "jIvajIva", "headword": "जीवजीव", "headword_slp1": "jIvajIva", "fold": "jivajiva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीवजीव m. the chakora bird.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीवजीवः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvajIvaH"]}], "jiv": [{"id": "jIv", "headword": "जीव्", "headword_slp1": "jIv", "fold": "jiv", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव् vi. 1P (pp. जीवित; pres. जीवति; caus. जीवयति, जीवापयति) 1. To live, to be alive, यावत् त्रयस्ते जीवेयुः M.ii.235, संशयं पुनारारुह्य यदि जीवति पश्यति Hit.i.; 2. to revive, to come to life; 3. to make a livelihood, to live by, (with an inst.), विपणेन च जीवंतः M.iii.152, iv.6 (in this sense, the root is sometimes used with a cognate acc., e.g. जीवेद्वैश्यस्य जीविकाम् M.x.82); 4. to live upon, to prey upon, (with a loc.), e.g. चौराः प्रमत्ते जीवंति व्याधितेषु चिकित्सकाः । प्रमदाः कामयानेषु यजमानेषु याजकाः । राजा विवदमानेषु नित्यं मूर्खेषु पंडिताः.With अति-, to surpass in living, to live more splendidly or happily, अत्यजीवदमरालकेश्वरौ R.xix.15.With अनु-, 1. to imitate the life of अन्वजीवत् (v.l. for अत्यजीवत्) अमरालकेश्वरौ R.xix.15; 2. to live for, to serve, to live by or by means of, (with an acc.), e.g. यां तां श्रियमसूयामः पुरा दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरे । अद्य तामनुजीवामः; 3. to survive, to outlive.With आ-, to get a living from, (with an acc.), e.g. यमाजीवंति पुरुषं सर्वभूतानि … … तस्य जीवितमर्थवत्.With उद्-, to return to life, to revive, उदजीवत् सुमित्राभूः Bt.xvii.95.With उप-, to maintain oneself by, (with an acc. of the person or profession), शेषास्तमुपजीवेयुर्यथैव पितरं तथा M.ix.105, संवाहकस्य वृत्तिमुपजीवामि Mrich.ii., Sis.ix.32.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "jiva": [{"id": "jIva", "headword": "जीव", "headword_slp1": "jIva", "fold": "jiva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव (I) a. (f. वा) Living, existing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "जीव (II) m. 1. The principle of life, the vital breath, श्वासोत्कंपकुचं निरीक्ष्य सुचिरं जीवाशया वारितः Am.S.90; 2. the personal soul cased in the body (as distinguished from the supreme soul or परमात्मन्), M.xii.22; 3. life, existence; 4. a creature, a living being; 5. livelihood, profession; 6. an epithet of Bṛhaspati; 7. an epithet of Karṇa; 8. the constellation called पुष्य.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीवः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvaH"]}, {"id": "jIvA", "headword": "जीवा", "headword_slp1": "jIvA", "fold": "jiva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव (I) a. (f. वा) Living, existing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "जीवा f. 1. Water; 2. the earth; 3. a bowstring, चापस्य जीवा चकृषे जवेन R.G.; 4. the chord of an arc; 5. means of living; 6. the tinkling of metallic ornaments.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "jivantaka": [{"id": "jIvAMtaka", "headword": "जीवांतक", "headword_slp1": "jIvAMtaka", "fold": "jivantaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव-अंतक m. 1. a bird-catcher, a fowler; 2. a murderer.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["जीवान्तक", "जीवान्तकः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["jIvAntaka", "jIvAntakaH"]}], "jivatman": [{"id": "jIvAtman", "headword": "जीवात्मन्", "headword_slp1": "jIvAtman", "fold": "jivatman", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव-आत्मन् m. the individual soul enshrined in the human body (as distinguished from परमात्मन् ‘the supreme soul’).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "jivadana": [{"id": "jIvAdAna", "headword": "जीवादान", "headword_slp1": "jIvAdAna", "fold": "jivadana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "जीव-आदान n. abstracting blood, bleeding (in medicine).", "gloss